hello_world.bin and partition-table.bin in this folder are the app image and partition
table from packages/scene/tests/fixtures/esp32s3-hello/firmware/. They were built from
packages/engine/tests/firmware/esp32s3/idf by packages/engine/scripts/esp32s3-firmware.sh
with ESP-IDF v5.5.5, the tag v5.5.5 of https://github.com/espressif/esp-idf, and its
toolchain esp-14.2.0_20260121. The partition table is that directory's partitions.csv.

The app image links ESP-IDF's components. They are under the Apache License 2.0, whose text is
LICENSE-APACHE at the root of this repository, apart from the files whose headers name other
terms. Among those, the FreeRTOS kernel is under the MIT License, reproduced with its notice in
LICENSE-freertos, and the Xtensa core HAL under the notice reproduced in LICENSE-xtensa. The
FreeRTOS Xtensa port and the Xtensa interrupt, context and vector files are under that same
notice, with the line Copyright (c) 2015-2019 Cadence Design Systems, Inc. The TLSF heap
allocator is under the BSD-3-Clause License, reproduced with its notice in LICENSE-tlsf, and the
undefined behaviour sanitizer hooks under the BSD-2-Clause terms reproduced with their notice in
LICENSE-ubsan. The image also holds routines of the toolchain's C library, newlib, under the
notices of LICENSE-newlib, and of the compiler's support library, under the GCC Runtime Library
Exception.

hello_world/main/hello_world_main.c is ESP-IDF's hello_world example, under CC0-1.0, with two
lines added.
